# Documentation maintenance

The documentation must reflect the actual state of the repository, not an idealized roadmap.

## Required practice

- When changing the CLI, data pipeline, model, schemas, deployment layout, or supported scenarios, update the relevant docs in README, AGENTS, and the docs site.
- Prefer references to concrete files and commands over generic statements.
- If a capability is only partially implemented, say so explicitly and mark it as partial or pending.
- When the mathematical formulation changes, update the mathematical documentation page and the summary in the landing page.
- Maintain a single source of truth for the long-term roadmap in docs/roadmap-aplicacion-despacho.md and mirror the current status in the site.

## Minimum check before finishing a change

- README and AGENTS mention the current architecture and workflows.
- The GitHub Pages site includes the changed feature or workflow.
- Any new BESS mode, CLI command, or solver assumption is documented with the corresponding evidence from the code.
